            evidence on screen yet and you'd just sound defensive.

            What you're setting up is the missing half: whether a good model
            on its own gets you there, or whether it still takes someone who
            knows how to work it. That's the question this whole talk answers,
            and the next three slides answer it with data rather than opinion.
          </aside>
        </section>

        <!-- 5b ──────────────────── INTERACTIVE BENCHMARK CHART (DeepSWE v1.1) -->
